# Everything works with this file empty. Nothing here is required.
#
# Previews and cover art come from Apple's public iTunes Search endpoint, which
# needs no account, no key and no token. `scripts/enrich-catalogue.mjs` already
# resolved every shipped track against it at build time.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: the Apple Music API (MusicKit)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setting these three switches the lookup in `src/lib/apple-music.ts` over to
# the official Apple Music catalogue instead. It buys slightly better matching
# and canonical music.apple.com links — and it costs a paid Apple Developer
# membership, which is why it is not the default.
#
# From developer.apple.com → Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles:
#   1. Keys → + → tick "MusicKit" → Continue → Register
#   2. Download the .p8 file (offered exactly once — keep it safe)
#   3. APPLE_KEY_ID  is the Key ID shown beside that key
#   4. APPLE_TEAM_ID is Membership details → Team ID
#   5. APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY is the .p8 file's contents, newlines written as \n
#
# Copy this file to .env.local to use it. .env.local and *.p8 are gitignored —
# the key is a credential and must never be committed.

# APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# APPLE_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIGT...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"

# Storefront to search, for both iTunes and MusicKit.
# "us" has the widest catalogue; "id" is Indonesia. Changing it after the
# catalogue has been enriched means re-running scripts/enrich-catalogue.mjs.
APPLE_STOREFRONT=us

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The one track in the corner
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to configure. It uses Apple's official embed, which needs no account,
# no token and no server call — set the song in src/data/music.ts instead.
#
# Anyone signed into Apple Music in their browser hears the full track; everyone
# else hears Apple's 30-second preview. There is no legal way to play a full
# commercial song to every visitor: a subscription is a right to listen, not a
# right to broadcast.
